-- Restaurant Tycoon 3 (place 119048529960596) - Matcha LuauVM
-- Version: 6.12.0 -- SERVE: confirmed by the plate leaving the tray, own thread
--
-- v6.11.0 report from the user: "good pickup, but it felt like it took forever to give the food
-- or like it never even gave it out". Both symptoms have ONE cause and it is a logic bug:
--
--   fire() returns pcall success, NOT server acceptance. FireServer on a RemoteEvent almost
--   never errors, so in 6.11.0 `local ok = serveToGuest(...)` was true on the FIRST attempt of
--   every dish. `landed = true` therefore fired immediately and GuestTriesPerDish = 3 was
--   never actually used - one blind attempt per dish per pass, at whatever guest serveIdx
--   happened to point at. When that guest was not waiting for that dish the server refused it
--   silently, the plate stayed in hand, and the next pass tried a different guest. That is
--   exactly "sometimes it works and it feels slow".
--
-- FIX: stop trusting the return value and look at the world instead.
--   ACCEPTED  <=>  the dish model is no longer a descendant of Tycoon.Objects.Food
-- (it is destroyed or reparented by the server when the hand-off lands). Each dish is now tried
-- against up to GuestAttemptsPerDish different guests until that test passes, then moves on.
--
-- Also in this version:
-- 1. Serve runs in its OWN loop (task.spawn), so a long serve pass can no longer stall bills,
--    dishes, orders, seating or tips - that shared loop was the "everything feels slow" part.
-- 2. Payload is EXACTLY the 6.8.0 one that the user confirmed works:
--      { FoodModel, Name='Serve', Tycoon, GroupId, CustomerId }
--    FoodName and FurnitureModel were added in 6.9.0/6.11.0 on a guess and are removed again.
-- 3. ServeGap 0.1 -> 0.06, and the serve loop waits only 0.15 s after a successful hand-off
--    (0.4 s when nothing landed) instead of a fixed 0.7 s cadence.
-- 4. Pair-cooldown bookkeeping dropped - it existed to work around the fake success above.
--    A dish that fails every guest is parked only 1.5 s.
-- 5. Tray detection kept: plates carrying Taken are the held ones (GrabFood.AttemptGrab sets
--    it); if no plate is flagged, every plate is tried.
--
-- Everything else is the user-confirmed 6.8.0: seating on ^T%d+$ only, tray prompt with no text
-- filter, ClassName-only part lookup, token bucket on the non-serve calls.
--
-- Call shapes (confirmed, differ - never assume uniformity):
--   bill  = Interacted THEN TaskCompleted 'CollectBill'   (2)
--   dish  = TaskCompleted 'CollectDishes'                 (1)
--   tips  = TipsCollected                                 (1)
--   order = TaskCompleted 'TakeOrder'                     (1)
--   seat  = TaskCompleted 'SendToTable'                   (1)
--   serve = fireproximityprompt (tray) then TaskCompleted 'Serve' per dish
--
-- Loader:
